From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:29:58 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: mock Neo WebGL identity and query limits natively

Expose a lightweight WebGL 1 query context from HTMLCanvasElement and
OffscreenCanvas, including worker globals. Keep native receiver checks,
method descriptors, context identity, canvas ownership and context-type
exclusion. Report live drawing-buffer dimensions without rendering work.

Use a synthetic Apple A18 Pro / ANGLE Metal identity for the base MacBook
Neo persona. Return numeric query limits and a fresh Int32Array viewport
limit through the existing typed-array bridge. These hardcoded limits are
chosen mock values, not measurements from a physical A18 Pro device.

Cache WEBGL_debug_renderer_info per context, gate its unmasked queries on
extension enablement, and return null plus clear-on-read INVALID_ENUM for
unsupported parameter queries. Advertise only the implemented debug
extension rather than the old stub's list of unimplemented extensions.
Expose query constants on the interface and its prototype.

Deliberately remain query-only: no rendering, shaders, buffers, textures,
WebGL2 or context-loss extension. Graphics consumers requiring resource
methods are not supported. Preserve the existing 2D paths and use their
empty synthetic PNG fallback for WebGL canvas exports.

Keep the benchmark unchanged: its modern-GPU allowlist recognizes Apple
M-series but not A18 Pro, so the GPU-limit assertion still cannot pass
with the required persona. Add no unit tests; validate with existing
upstream tests and ignored temporary page/iframe/worker CDP diagnostics.

References:
https://www.apple.com/macbook-neo/specs/
https://registry.khronos.org/webgl/specs/latest/1.0/
https://registry.khronos.org/webgl/extensions/WEBGL_debug_renderer_info/
